    "solution": "Jump and dash beneath the west overhang onto the small pressure-pod island. Jump past its right edge, then dash diagonally down-left back into the pod: it reverses that approach into an up-right throw and returns the dash. Spend the restored dash straight up through the now-open phase bridge. Cut upward at the bell near the apex to put the bridge back beneath you. The entire eastern gallery is then a safe walk out.",
    "nearestExisting": "F34 uses a wallbounce and an aerial phase bell. This chamber instead makes the approach direction to a pressure pod and the parity of two successive dashes inseparable: the return launch must clear an island lip, spend a recovered dash through the bridge, then restore the bridge with the blade.",
    "novelty": "The apparent destination is a low island directly beneath a bridge that cannot be reached from a normal dash. The solution first moves away from the exit, approaching the pressure pod from its far side so its recoil returns both useful direction and a fresh dash. The final blade input changes the same bridge just crossed, and the landing is seven tiles wide followed by the whole exit floor.",
